WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:00.100 --> 00:06.070
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series

4
00:06.110 --> 00:08.750
are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

5
00:08.790 --> 00:13.280
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

6
00:13.320 --> 00:15.720
Viewer discretion is advised.

7
00:16.200 --> 00:18.040
We've always stuck together lately.

8
00:18.200 --> 00:19.680
Then you two should spend some time apart.

9
00:19.720 --> 00:21.270
Chan, you know what you need to do, right?

10
00:21.310 --> 00:23.050
There’s nothing I need to worry about, right?

11
00:23.230 --> 00:24.920
About your mom,

12
00:25.050 --> 00:27.040
she is the real last boss, like Sun said.

13
00:27.470 --> 00:28.400
You are sick?

14
00:28.440 --> 00:30.570
I want someone to take care of me right now.

15
00:30.600 --> 00:32.009
You want me to stay and take care of you?

16
00:34.340 --> 00:36.450
Does it suit your palate, Mom?

17
00:36.730 --> 00:39.770
But I believe that you can win her over.

18
00:39.990 --> 00:42.250
We are only going to take our hatred out on each other.

19
00:42.370 --> 00:43.690
Don’t you feel sorry for Chan?

20
00:43.850 --> 00:46.440
Why do we have to hate each other?

21
00:52.490 --> 00:53.450
Mom.

22
00:56.090 --> 00:57.400
I love you.

23
00:58.990 --> 01:01.040
I invited you to join me today.

24
01:01.660 --> 01:03.580
Because I want you…

25
01:05.120 --> 01:07.680
to be present in the most important moment of my life.

26
01:50.310 --> 01:52.300
I will use these earrings

27
01:54.500 --> 01:55.900
to propose to you.

28
01:58.310 --> 01:59.850
My proposal is simple.

29
02:00.400 --> 02:01.900
It’s nothing special.

30
02:02.900 --> 02:04.900
I didn’t throw a big event

31
02:05.870 --> 02:07.180
like I always do.

32
02:16.250 --> 02:18.100
I just want to show you

33
02:21.180 --> 02:23.400
that I’m doing this out of my genuine love.

34
02:31.570 --> 02:33.300
We don’t need a grand gesture

35
02:37.320 --> 02:38.900
or an extravagant event.

36
02:44.210 --> 02:46.300
I will use these earrings

37
02:48.590 --> 02:50.200
to propose to you.

38
02:58.490 --> 03:00.170
Will you marry me, Key?

39
03:44.520 --> 03:45.800
Thank you.

40
05:05.440 --> 05:07.490
Don’t you think this is too much?

41
05:08.350 --> 05:10.550
You fired Key’s band from the bar.

42
05:11.440 --> 05:13.130
Just because she’s my fiancée.

43
05:14.610 --> 05:15.900
I already made up my mind.

44
05:16.190 --> 05:17.800
I also found a new band.

45
05:21.690 --> 05:22.700
Mrs. Chanya.

46
05:23.070 --> 05:25.420
Miss Key’s band is very popular.

47
05:25.460 --> 05:26.330
So what?

48
05:27.300 --> 05:29.350
The new band is also talented.

49
05:30.270 --> 05:31.800
They have their fan base.

50
05:32.170 --> 05:34.350
Are you sure you’re going to do this?

51
05:34.730 --> 05:36.540
I’m doing this for our hotel’s interests.

52
05:37.530 --> 05:38.500
It’s not true.

53
05:39.380 --> 05:41.270
You’re not doing this for the hotel.

54
05:42.490 --> 05:45.000
You’re doing this to pressure me.

55
05:53.070 --> 05:54.270
It’s okay, Chan.

56
05:56.120 --> 05:57.270
That’s enough.

57
05:59.090 --> 06:00.500
I’m sorry, Key.

58
06:01.420 --> 06:03.920
This is not fair to you and your bandmates.

59
06:06.590 --> 06:08.520
They won’t have a problem with it.

60
06:16.590 --> 06:21.000
You’re not going to get your way with us by doing this.

61
06:22.650 --> 06:24.320
I’m doing everything for you.

62
06:24.800 --> 06:28.410
When will you understand that she is not a good match for you?

63
06:30.150 --> 06:34.000
Who gets to decide who is right for me?

64
06:35.750 --> 06:37.500
Only your opinion matters?

65
06:39.710 --> 06:41.100
My partner,

66
06:42.550 --> 06:44.600
I can’t even choose that myself?

67
06:45.840 --> 06:47.800
Do you love her more than me, Chan?

68
06:48.500 --> 06:49.690
Why are you so against me?

69
06:49.840 --> 06:51.000
Mom.

70
06:59.120 --> 07:00.950
You’ve changed since you met Key.

71
07:02.300 --> 07:04.170
You are not the same daughter I used to know.

72
07:07.540 --> 07:08.500
Chan.

73
07:08.890 --> 07:09.700
I think…

74
07:09.740 --> 07:10.900
Let’s leave, Key.

75
07:18.040 --> 07:18.690
Miss Chan.

76
07:18.730 --> 07:19.760
Don’t follow her.

77
07:27.340 --> 07:30.030
Bring me all the documents for today’s meeting.

78
07:31.320 --> 07:32.700
Yes, Mrs. Chanya.

79
07:57.030 --> 07:58.100
Wait, Chan.

80
08:01.850 --> 08:02.800
I think…

81
08:03.880 --> 08:05.520
this is getting out of hand.

82
08:07.190 --> 08:10.600
Your mom will never accept me.

83
08:14.360 --> 08:15.700
Are you giving up?

84
08:19.940 --> 08:21.720
But I’m putting you in a tight spot.

85
08:23.570 --> 08:25.170
I don’t want to be selfish

86
08:26.080 --> 08:27.930
and cause a rift between you and your mom.

87
08:29.010 --> 08:30.520
Then don’t give up.

88
08:32.330 --> 08:33.730
Don’t leave me.

89
08:39.289 --> 08:41.500
I will never give up on you.

90
08:44.190 --> 08:47.970
I believe that we will find a way to win my mom over

91
08:49.560 --> 08:51.300
as long as we hold onto each other.

92
08:58.020 --> 08:59.070
I love this.

93
09:00.790 --> 09:02.550
My fiancée is so cool.

94
09:03.650 --> 09:05.000
This is so touching.

95
09:05.620 --> 09:07.050
Stop joking around.

96
09:08.290 --> 09:09.700
I can’t help it.

97
09:10.760 --> 09:12.100
You are so cool.

98
09:19.000 --> 09:20.470
Promise me.

99
09:21.550 --> 09:23.700
You will never give up on us.

100
09:25.940 --> 09:27.100
Fine.

101
09:28.290 --> 09:29.500
Stop nagging me.

102
09:31.350 --> 09:32.430
I promise.

103
09:50.050 --> 09:54.240
Thank you for accepting me into your family.

104
09:56.150 --> 09:59.700
If Key loves you, we all love you too.

105
10:04.370 --> 10:09.050
About your mom, what are you going to do?

106
10:11.110 --> 10:11.900
Yes.

107
10:12.280 --> 10:14.030
That’s the only thing I’m worried about.

108
10:14.500 --> 10:16.200
If this is not resolved,

109
10:16.710 --> 10:18.700
you two will never be happy.

110
10:19.980 --> 10:22.910
About that, Chan and I,

111
10:23.580 --> 10:26.000
we are counting on a silver bullet to solve the problem.

112
10:26.730 --> 10:27.700
A silver bullet?

113
10:28.530 --> 10:30.200
What is it?

114
10:35.350 --> 10:36.250
Wait.

115
10:36.860 --> 10:41.700
Tell me who came up with the plan?

116
10:44.110 --> 10:45.160
It’s Chan’s plan.

117
10:45.980 --> 10:47.240
She’s her mom.

118
10:48.660 --> 10:50.330
Chan knows how to work her way around her mom.

119
10:52.750 --> 10:55.700
What is the silver bullet?

120
10:59.190 --> 11:04.370
It’s someone no one would have expected.

121
12:34.950 --> 12:37.270
Mom, please take care of Simba for me.

122
12:39.990 --> 12:41.380
You know I’m allergic to cats.

123
12:41.420 --> 12:43.120
Why did you leave it with me?

124
12:49.610 --> 12:51.100
So your name is Simba?

125
12:51.670 --> 12:52.610
Where are you going?

126
12:57.290 --> 12:59.550
You will leave a scratch on the chair.

127
13:00.240 --> 13:00.940
Hey.

128
13:02.190 --> 13:02.900
Hey.

129
13:04.520 --> 13:07.300
Why are you scratching? Do you have a skin disease?

130
13:09.280 --> 13:11.560
Get off the chair.

131
13:12.190 --> 13:13.100
Do you hear me?

132
13:13.880 --> 13:15.270
Get down to the floor.

133
13:16.840 --> 13:18.940
Get down to the floor.

134
13:21.940 --> 13:23.310
You understand my words.

135
13:24.690 --> 13:26.300
Don’t go up to the white sofa.

136
13:31.400 --> 13:32.200
Hey.

137
13:34.970 --> 13:36.200
Are you heading to my room?

138
13:36.240 --> 13:38.080
Don’t go into my room. Come out.

139
13:39.490 --> 13:41.350
What the hell?!

140
13:42.980 --> 13:44.270
Gosh!

141
13:53.280 --> 13:54.090
Meow.

142
13:55.080 --> 13:55.850
Meow.

143
14:00.330 --> 14:01.420
Meow, meow.

144
14:07.130 --> 14:08.100
What is this?

145
14:19.290 --> 14:22.400
Why did you ask me to meet you if you are going to say nothing?

146
14:26.940 --> 14:28.550
I just want you to sit with me.

147
14:30.920 --> 14:33.070
I’ve been sitting here for almost an hour.

148
14:36.920 --> 14:42.800
So this is what it feels like to watch my ex getting married.

149
14:47.170 --> 14:49.000
Chan probably felt the same back then.

150
14:51.070 --> 14:52.500
She was in a much worse shape than you.

151
14:52.590 --> 14:53.900
I saw it with my own eyes.

152
14:58.890 --> 15:00.700
I guess karma is catching up with me.

153
15:03.870 --> 15:04.850
You are being extra.

154
15:06.640 --> 15:07.700
You’re so extra.

155
15:13.770 --> 15:15.200
I’ll go to the bathroom and be right back.

156
15:47.130 --> 15:48.570
Do you also drink coffee?

157
15:48.950 --> 15:50.450
I thought you drank only alcohol.

158
16:01.470 --> 16:03.560
Your ex is getting married.

159
16:04.230 --> 16:06.120
Is that why you look dejected?

160
16:16.280 --> 16:17.200
I know that.

161
16:17.680 --> 16:18.690
You don’t need to remind me.

162
16:19.350 --> 16:22.600
I said that because I want you to face the truth.

163
16:25.030 --> 16:26.100
Can I ask you something?

164
16:26.620 --> 16:28.700
How long are you going to hold on to your ex?

165
16:30.470 --> 16:31.500
That’s none of your business.

166
16:35.190 --> 16:38.500
I’m saying this because I mean well.

167
16:47.870 --> 16:49.400
Can’t I feel sad for a while?

168
16:50.510 --> 16:52.110
I will get over it eventually.

169
16:52.710 --> 16:54.500
I still have my pride.

170
17:00.870 --> 17:02.500
So you are feeling down

171
17:03.120 --> 17:05.000
because you are trying to get over her?

172
17:11.930 --> 17:12.849
I like that.

173
17:13.250 --> 17:14.069
What?

174
17:17.460 --> 17:20.200
I mean, I like that you are trying to get over her.

175
17:20.380 --> 17:21.950
That’s an improvement.

176
17:25.849 --> 17:27.300
I don’t understand you.

177
17:28.020 --> 17:29.300
What do you want from me?

178
17:29.490 --> 17:30.890
Why are you meddling in my business?

179
17:31.180 --> 17:32.380
I have a lot of free time.

180
17:32.710 --> 17:34.200
I’m doing this to kill time.

181
17:44.130 --> 17:45.570
Come on. Get up.

182
17:48.160 --> 17:49.100
Where are we going?

183
17:50.660 --> 17:52.000
I’ll give you a reward.

184
17:52.420 --> 17:53.400
I’ll buy you a meal.

185
17:53.970 --> 17:54.830
No.

186
17:55.310 --> 17:56.530
I came here with Phu.

187
17:57.510 --> 17:58.300
It’s okay.

188
17:59.350 --> 18:00.130
You can go with her.

189
18:03.620 --> 18:04.400
Come on.

190
18:04.880 --> 18:05.600
Get up.

191
18:05.860 --> 18:07.570
Wear your glasses to look pretty.

192
18:09.650 --> 18:10.570
I can do it myself.

193
18:14.050 --> 18:15.430
Come on. Get up.

194
18:16.690 --> 18:17.810
I can get up by myself.

195
18:18.550 --> 18:20.380
If you could, why didn’t you get up sooner?

196
18:22.190 --> 18:23.100
Your coffee.

197
18:24.210 --> 18:25.700
-Which way? -That way.

198
18:27.720 --> 18:28.520
See you.

199
18:30.500 --> 18:33.300
Jay needs someone like this.

200
18:41.960 --> 18:44.380
This is where you wanted to take me.

201
18:45.870 --> 18:48.300
Everyone always celebrates with Moo Krata.

202
18:49.470 --> 18:51.500
Grilled meat is bad for our health.

203
18:52.780 --> 18:55.000
You are concerned about your health?

204
18:55.450 --> 18:56.840
But you get drunk every day.

205
18:57.580 --> 18:58.570
What an irony.

206
19:06.150 --> 19:07.080
Can you help fan?

207
19:07.110 --> 19:08.380
The fire is dying down.

208
19:08.800 --> 19:09.810
Don’t make me do all the work.

209
19:14.460 --> 19:16.500
Why do you go through this trouble?

210
19:17.570 --> 19:19.770
Why didn’t you have them grill it for you?

211
19:27.930 --> 19:30.200
You need to step out of your comfort zone.

212
19:30.910 --> 19:33.000
Maybe you’ll get new perspectives.

213
19:36.990 --> 19:38.870
Stop acting like you’re a life coach.

214
19:39.040 --> 19:40.160
I’m not falling for it.

215
19:44.110 --> 19:46.600
Stop acting like you’re a life coach. I’m not falling for it.

216
19:46.640 --> 19:48.900
Stop talking and eat it.

217
19:53.770 --> 19:54.900
Try it.

218
19:56.550 --> 19:58.770
-It’s burnt. -Just eat it.

219
20:02.590 --> 20:04.300
Come on. It won’t kill you.

220
20:05.480 --> 20:06.400
Try it.

221
20:31.540 --> 20:32.650
What are you looking at?

222
20:33.310 --> 20:34.100
What?

223
20:35.250 --> 20:37.010
I’m looking at you eating. How is it?

224
20:37.050 --> 20:38.000
Is it good?

225
20:40.250 --> 20:41.980
It tastes good, doesn’t it?

226
20:56.200 --> 20:58.310
From the look, I didn’t think it would taste good.

227
21:00.370 --> 21:03.900
You little princess, you’ve been living in your ivory tower for too long.

228
21:05.400 --> 21:06.300
Hey.

229
21:07.010 --> 21:08.870
You need to step out and see the real world.

230
21:14.600 --> 21:17.090
I just never had a chance to eat it.

231
21:18.610 --> 21:21.000
If you keep holding on to the same old things

232
21:21.090 --> 21:22.700
and cling to the past,

233
21:23.080 --> 21:24.560
you’ll never know

234
21:24.820 --> 21:27.600
if there is something better waiting for you.

235
21:31.370 --> 21:33.600
Stop expecting your life to be perfect.

236
21:34.990 --> 21:38.300
Even if your life is not perfect, it’s not that terrible.

237
21:40.800 --> 21:43.300
Learning to live with your small mistakes

238
21:44.320 --> 21:45.570
is not a bad thing.

239
21:48.520 --> 21:49.700
Are you hitting on me?

240
21:51.490 --> 21:53.500
I’m saying this because I want to be your friend.

241
21:56.120 --> 21:57.700
As your new friend,

242
21:58.550 --> 22:00.670
I want you to stop clinging to the past.

243
22:01.880 --> 22:03.580
If you keep doing this,

244
22:06.620 --> 22:08.600
you may lose Chan as a friend.

245
22:11.950 --> 22:14.900
You need to face the truth and let it go.

246
22:17.830 --> 22:19.970
Don’t you want to have Chan in your life as a friend?

247
22:21.710 --> 22:24.000
Do you really want to lose a good friend like her?

248
22:43.860 --> 22:44.700
Here.

249
22:45.340 --> 22:46.300
I’ll feed you.

250
22:50.130 --> 22:51.580
Why do I have to eat it?

251
22:52.150 --> 22:53.980
It’s grilled pork for our sworn friendship.

252
22:54.020 --> 22:56.750
This will be an official beginning of our friendship.

253
23:01.960 --> 23:02.770
Here.

254
23:14.090 --> 23:14.970
Come on.

255
23:16.650 --> 23:17.600
It’s hot.

256
23:27.260 --> 23:28.100
Here.

257
23:32.450 --> 23:33.600
Just eat it.

258
23:44.410 --> 23:45.580
Feed me too.

259
23:48.510 --> 23:50.430
Come on. I’m hungry.

260
23:50.450 --> 23:51.950
I haven’t taken a single bite.

261
23:52.310 --> 23:53.980
You are the only one who is eating.

262
24:00.280 --> 24:01.650
I like my pork well-done.

263
24:15.270 --> 24:17.100
That piece is fine.

264
24:17.660 --> 24:18.700
I can eat it.

265
24:20.920 --> 24:22.000
Blow it for me.

266
24:23.380 --> 24:24.900
Come on. It’s hot.

267
24:26.820 --> 24:28.140
Come on. It’s hot.

268
24:37.180 --> 24:38.200
Ahh.

269
24:44.060 --> 24:44.970
It’s delicious.

270
24:47.730 --> 24:50.700
The new friendship ceremony is complete.

271
24:55.030 --> 24:56.600
You are strange.

272
24:56.810 --> 24:58.000
You are strange.

273
24:58.140 --> 24:59.670
How can you never have eaten Moo Krata before?

274
24:59.710 --> 25:03.230
This piece is only for my loved one.

275
25:05.990 --> 25:07.040
Do you love me?

276
25:08.690 --> 25:09.800
I love you as a friend.

277
25:27.140 --> 25:29.100
If you want to smile, just smile.

278
25:38.140 --> 25:39.200
Let’s do a test.

279
25:39.580 --> 25:41.560
If you are Thai, you won’t spit it out.

280
25:41.710 --> 25:42.490
Come on.

281
25:44.830 --> 25:46.000
I can eat it myself.

282
25:54.610 --> 25:56.310
If you want to laugh, just laugh.

283
25:56.350 --> 25:57.490
No need to hold it in.

284
25:59.680 --> 26:01.400
You look cute when you laugh.

285
26:22.550 --> 26:23.300
Key.

286
26:24.790 --> 26:25.700
What?

287
26:27.640 --> 26:29.000
Why are you making that face?

288
26:30.110 --> 26:32.000
I was wrong about Mom.

289
26:33.660 --> 26:34.600
Why?

290
26:35.130 --> 26:37.670
I don’t know where she took Simba.

291
26:38.140 --> 26:40.500
I checked the home security camera. No one is home.

292
26:46.740 --> 26:47.600
Simba.

293
26:48.320 --> 26:49.300
Simba.

294
26:49.620 --> 26:50.870
Simba, where are you?

295
26:54.800 --> 26:56.520
-Simba. -Simba.

296
26:57.280 --> 26:58.780
Simba, Mommy is back.

297
26:59.190 --> 27:00.200
Where are you?

298
27:00.910 --> 27:01.800
Simba.

299
27:07.210 --> 27:09.580
I never thought she would do this.

300
27:11.750 --> 27:12.960
Calm down, Chan.

301
27:13.560 --> 27:16.900
I don’t think your mom would do anything to him.

302
27:22.560 --> 27:24.300
Do you think…

303
27:25.590 --> 27:27.200
I’m just afraid that

304
27:27.950 --> 27:30.200
my mom is so determined to make me give in

305
27:32.090 --> 27:33.900
that she doesn’t care about anything else.

306
27:35.720 --> 27:38.000
Do you think she can be that cruel?

307
27:40.960 --> 27:42.700
When we had problems,

308
27:43.600 --> 27:45.900
she's never been this drastic.

309
27:47.190 --> 27:48.500
But this time,

310
27:50.110 --> 27:52.560
I might be wrong about her.

311
28:00.530 --> 28:01.400
Mom.

312
28:01.720 --> 28:03.010
What are you making that face?

313
28:03.180 --> 28:04.790
Where is Simba?

314
28:05.170 --> 28:06.250
He’s right here.

315
28:07.840 --> 28:09.900
Where did you take him?

316
28:10.260 --> 28:11.690
Why didn’t you tell me first?

317
28:11.850 --> 28:13.700
I called you, but you didn’t answer my calls.

318
28:13.890 --> 28:15.440
I didn’t want to talk to you.

319
28:16.450 --> 28:18.290
Why did you take Simba with you?

320
28:20.090 --> 28:21.300
I took him to a groomer.

321
28:22.780 --> 28:23.560
Huh?

322
28:24.120 --> 28:27.500
Did you really take him to a groomer?

323
28:28.590 --> 28:29.800
Yes.

324
28:30.630 --> 28:32.880
I also bought a new cat tower for him.

325
28:33.940 --> 28:36.620
I ordered an automatic litter box for him.

326
28:36.660 --> 28:37.900
It will be delivered soon.

327
28:38.320 --> 28:41.030
I bought outfits for the rainy season and winter.

328
28:41.470 --> 28:42.760
He doesn’t need outfits for summer.

329
28:42.960 --> 28:44.900
I also bought outfits for his airport looks.

330
28:45.410 --> 28:46.920
Can you go get them from my car?

331
28:49.740 --> 28:50.640
What?

332
28:51.420 --> 28:53.000
Don’t you hear it?

333
28:53.670 --> 28:55.970
Go to my car and bring his stuff here.

334
28:56.010 --> 28:57.200
So he can try his outfits.

335
29:00.160 --> 29:01.700
Yes. Sure.

336
29:10.100 --> 29:11.600
Sweetie.

337
29:11.950 --> 29:12.910
Yes, Mom.

338
29:14.270 --> 29:15.060
Huh?

339
29:17.520 --> 29:19.000
I’m not talking to you, Chan.

340
29:21.310 --> 29:23.240
Right, sweetie?

341
29:24.440 --> 29:26.380
Are you tired?

342
29:28.900 --> 29:30.650
Are you no longer allergic to animal fur?

343
29:31.760 --> 29:33.300
Yes, I still am.

344
29:34.080 --> 29:37.180
But I’m not allergic to Simba’s fur.

345
29:40.300 --> 29:41.200
Right?

346
29:41.660 --> 29:44.300
I’m not allergic to your fur.

347
29:44.940 --> 29:47.100
You must feel really sleepy.

348
29:47.860 --> 29:49.180
You turn into jelly.

349
29:49.940 --> 29:51.500
Okay, okay.

350
29:56.390 --> 29:58.420
Simba doesn’t seem to want to be with you.

351
29:58.460 --> 29:59.600
He loves me.

352
30:00.040 --> 30:01.830
He loves me very much.

353
30:01.870 --> 30:03.940
He loves and adores me.

354
30:03.980 --> 30:05.040
Am I right?

355
30:07.510 --> 30:09.200
What do you want to talk to me about?

356
30:09.870 --> 30:11.000
It’s about Key.

357
30:11.290 --> 30:12.760
What else is there to talk about?

358
30:13.130 --> 30:14.380
About my marriage.

359
30:15.630 --> 30:17.500
Key is the only one I will marry.

360
30:23.250 --> 30:25.880
If you want to have my blessing in marriage,

361
30:29.020 --> 30:30.500
I have a condition.

362
30:34.250 --> 30:36.870
Are you going to take Simba from us?

363
30:37.400 --> 30:38.580
Are you crazy?

364
30:39.200 --> 30:40.680
What kind of person do you think I am?

365
30:43.450 --> 30:47.060
What is your condition?

366
30:49.040 --> 30:51.600
Key must go live with me for one week.

367
30:53.440 --> 30:55.600
So I can thoroughly evaluate her.

368
30:57.920 --> 30:58.800
Sure.

369
31:01.970 --> 31:03.200
That’s not all.

370
31:05.230 --> 31:10.200
You may want to say no after hearing my rule.

371
31:12.410 --> 31:13.450
Rule?

372
31:14.670 --> 31:15.600
What is it?

373
31:18.050 --> 31:23.600
You can’t contact Chan at all while you are living with me.

374
31:26.500 --> 31:27.580
Why?

375
31:28.950 --> 31:31.440
Why are you forbidding me to contact her?

376
31:31.700 --> 31:33.450
If you can’t do it, then we no longer need to talk.

377
31:33.560 --> 31:34.600
I can do it.

378
31:35.130 --> 31:36.240
I’ll do it.

379
31:39.190 --> 31:40.300
When will we go?

380
31:42.140 --> 31:43.170
Today.

381
31:44.610 --> 31:46.000
Right now.

382
31:47.120 --> 31:47.970
Mom.

383
31:48.460 --> 31:49.700
I have one more condition.

384
31:50.340 --> 31:51.500
What is it?

385
31:54.160 --> 31:55.500
I’ll take Simba with me.

386
32:01.480 --> 32:02.500
Sure.

387
32:04.730 --> 32:05.600
No.

388
32:06.340 --> 32:07.300
I won’t do it.

389
32:08.280 --> 32:09.650
Then who am I going to be with?

390
32:10.230 --> 32:13.180
If you feel lonely, I’ll tell Mam to come and stay with you.

391
32:18.590 --> 32:21.850
If she doesn’t pass my evaluation,

392
32:23.910 --> 32:25.280
I won’t allow you two to get married.

393
32:28.410 --> 32:29.450
I’ll do it.

394
32:31.280 --> 32:32.810
But I have one condition.

395
32:35.940 --> 32:36.940
What is it?

396
32:39.770 --> 32:42.400
Can I call you Mom?

397
32:50.170 --> 32:51.700
If you pass my evaluation,

398
32:54.300 --> 32:56.200
I’ll let you call me Mom.

399
32:59.610 --> 33:01.900
Okay. That’s fair enough.

400
33:02.790 --> 33:04.760
We have a deal, Mom.

401
33:06.880 --> 33:08.700
I mean, Madam.

402
33:48.220 --> 33:49.300
So…

403
33:50.670 --> 33:52.840
Key is living with your mom, just the two of them.

404
33:53.260 --> 33:55.670
Yes, and with the cat.

405
33:57.340 --> 33:58.500
That’s a good sign.

406
33:59.530 --> 34:00.500
I know.

407
34:01.880 --> 34:04.580
But she doesn’t allow me to talk to Key at all.

408
34:04.620 --> 34:06.000
That’s what I’m worried about.

409
34:08.310 --> 34:09.199
Come on.

410
34:09.909 --> 34:10.900
Hang in there.

411
34:12.199 --> 34:13.409
To get her blessing in marriage.

412
34:14.870 --> 34:15.800
Fine.

413
34:21.370 --> 34:22.300
Right.

414
34:24.510 --> 34:25.600
About Jay,

415
34:27.670 --> 34:29.300
you don’t need to worry anymore.

416
34:31.600 --> 34:33.580
I think she is getting over you.

417
34:39.150 --> 34:44.500
I hope that you and Jay can be friends again.

418
34:48.520 --> 34:50.120
I want us to hang out together.

419
34:56.199 --> 34:57.000
Yes.

420
35:03.010 --> 35:04.700
Come on. Let’s go have dinner.

421
35:04.860 --> 35:05.800
Don’t worry.

422
35:06.980 --> 35:08.500
I’m sure Key can handle your mom.

423
37:31.610 --> 37:33.290
Key will be fine, Chan.

424
37:35.800 --> 37:39.580
I’m sure she can win your mom over.

425
37:40.830 --> 37:42.100
She is a nice girl.

426
37:42.870 --> 37:45.650
Everyone who gets to know her can’t help but fall for her.

427
37:50.170 --> 37:51.100
Chan.

428
37:52.360 --> 37:54.400
You must miss her very much, right?

429
39:35.300 --> 39:36.700
You are holding me tight.

430
39:39.270 --> 39:40.700
It’s because I miss you.

431
39:41.230 --> 39:42.670
You need to hold me back.

432
39:45.960 --> 39:47.900
I miss you too.

433
40:03.620 --> 40:04.600
How was it?

434
40:05.340 --> 40:06.900
Did you win my mom over?

435
40:09.960 --> 40:11.210
Mom?

436
40:13.590 --> 40:15.100
You call her Mom.

437
40:15.510 --> 40:17.170
It means that you did it.

438
40:19.980 --> 40:21.700
Thanks to Simba.

439
40:22.450 --> 40:24.100
She’s falling hard for him.

440
40:25.290 --> 40:27.300
If she got upset, I just handed her the cat.

441
40:27.520 --> 40:29.520
Soon she would forget it.

442
40:31.030 --> 40:32.050
Is that so?

443
40:35.300 --> 40:36.800
Where is Simba?

444
40:37.310 --> 40:39.100
I miss him too.

445
40:39.330 --> 40:42.450
Your mom wants him to stay with her for a few more days.

446
40:45.650 --> 40:47.920
Be careful. She might take him to live with her.

447
40:51.450 --> 40:53.000
I feel bad for her.

448
40:53.620 --> 40:57.700
She built a cage so he can enjoy the garden.

449
41:01.430 --> 41:05.400
I guess we need to adopt another cat.

450
41:26.560 --> 41:27.750
I miss you so much.

451
41:35.580 --> 41:37.800
Please stay with me like this every day.

452
41:45.280 --> 41:47.230
Just waking up to see you,

453
41:49.830 --> 41:53.600
it already makes me feel happy.

454
41:57.810 --> 41:58.930
Me too.

455
42:01.420 --> 42:02.800
My Chan.

456
42:26.920 --> 42:28.200
I miss you.

457
42:44.850 --> 42:48.000
Key, where do you want to go for our honeymoon?

458
42:48.720 --> 42:51.760
Do you want to go to Europe or Asia?

459
42:52.590 --> 42:53.800
Anywhere is fine with me.

460
42:54.240 --> 42:56.410
I can go anywhere as long as you go with me.

461
42:57.380 --> 42:59.600
Of course, I will go with you.

462
43:05.700 --> 43:07.300
In Europe,

463
43:08.550 --> 43:10.650
which countries have you not visited yet?

464
43:11.650 --> 43:13.200
Europe?

465
43:14.270 --> 43:15.850
I have been to several countries.

466
43:17.540 --> 43:18.930
I traveled a lot.

467
43:24.540 --> 43:25.840
Who did you travel with?

468
43:27.120 --> 43:28.080
I…

469
43:30.480 --> 43:31.640
With Jay?

470
43:34.650 --> 43:37.700
Can I be jealous?

471
43:38.310 --> 43:39.500
Yes, you can.

472
43:40.650 --> 43:42.100
But don’t be mad at me.

473
43:43.210 --> 43:44.500
Why?

474
43:46.190 --> 43:47.670
I’m not good at making up.

475
43:50.010 --> 43:51.500
Then I’ll be mad at you.

476
43:52.160 --> 43:53.800
So you will get better at making up.

477
43:59.970 --> 44:01.100
I’m sorry.

478
44:02.450 --> 44:03.600
I was wrong.

479
44:04.840 --> 44:06.100
Please don’t be mad at me.

480
44:07.520 --> 44:08.700
I’m still mad at you.

481
44:14.170 --> 44:16.330
Please stop being mad at me, pretty girl.

482
44:17.530 --> 44:18.300
Please.

483
44:19.360 --> 44:20.960
You need to do more than that.

484
44:31.390 --> 44:32.800
I’m sorry.

485
44:34.490 --> 44:35.800
Don’t be mad at me.

486
44:37.000 --> 44:38.900
From now on,

487
44:39.870 --> 44:42.300
I’ll take you on lots of vacations.

488
44:42.820 --> 44:47.900
More than I’ve ever taken anyone else on.

489
44:48.560 --> 44:49.400
Alright.

490
44:53.970 --> 44:54.900
You are smiling.

491
44:58.190 --> 45:00.500
Can you talk to me like you’re a big sister?

492
45:01.560 --> 45:03.000
Big sister and little sister.

493
45:08.460 --> 45:09.920
If I do that,

494
45:10.930 --> 45:12.330
will you stop being mad at me?

495
45:14.630 --> 45:15.500
I don’t know.

496
45:15.920 --> 45:17.300
We’ll have to wait and see.

497
45:17.410 --> 45:19.100
If I like what I hear.

498
45:25.560 --> 45:27.100
I’m sorry.

499
45:28.900 --> 45:30.300
Please don’t be mad at me.

500
45:32.480 --> 45:33.800
I love you.

501
45:41.850 --> 45:42.900
Okay.

502
45:43.410 --> 45:44.760
I’ll let it slide.

503
46:03.240 --> 46:04.300
You can answer her call.

504
46:04.650 --> 46:05.600
I’m okay.

505
46:08.450 --> 46:10.090
Are you really okay with it?

506
46:11.580 --> 46:12.400
Yes.

507
46:13.280 --> 46:15.920
I trust you.

508
46:30.100 --> 46:31.180
Hello, Jay.

509
46:41.240 --> 46:43.800
Thank you for coming to see me.

510
46:45.270 --> 46:46.650
I thought you wouldn’t come.

511
46:47.560 --> 46:49.690
Because you were afraid that Key would feel uncomfortable.

512
46:53.050 --> 46:54.400
She is okay with it.

513
46:55.330 --> 46:56.500
To be honest,

514
46:57.490 --> 46:59.370
she was the one who told me to meet you.

515
47:00.280 --> 47:04.200
So I should thank her

516
47:05.420 --> 47:07.520
for convincing you to meet me.

517
47:12.430 --> 47:13.650
I mean it.

518
47:14.000 --> 47:15.230
I’m not being sarcastic.

519
47:20.520 --> 47:24.100
You said you had something important to tell me.

520
47:25.840 --> 47:26.780
What is it?

521
47:34.960 --> 47:36.770
The last time we talked,

522
47:38.700 --> 47:40.200
you told me

523
47:43.880 --> 47:46.050
you wanted me to go back to being the old me.

524
47:50.870 --> 47:52.300
I made up my mind.

525
47:53.980 --> 47:56.220
I’m going back to being the old Jay.

526
48:00.270 --> 48:03.450
I’m glad to hear that.

527
48:09.270 --> 48:11.100
I want to clear the air

528
48:12.150 --> 48:14.000
for your peace of mind

529
48:15.450 --> 48:16.930
and mine as well.

530
48:22.380 --> 48:26.700
All that time, I was holding on to the past.

531
48:28.740 --> 48:31.070
I did everything to get you back.

532
48:34.900 --> 48:36.860
I put you in a difficult position.

533
48:38.410 --> 48:40.200
It was also painful for me.

534
48:44.020 --> 48:45.400
Now I know…

535
48:47.100 --> 48:48.870
what the right thing is.

536
48:51.940 --> 48:53.800
The right thing is…

537
48:54.650 --> 48:56.150
I have to let you go.

538
48:57.750 --> 48:59.700
So that I can start a new chapter.

539
49:12.030 --> 49:13.200
I’m sorry…

540
49:15.330 --> 49:17.200
for everything I did to you.

541
49:22.730 --> 49:28.000
Both back then and now.

542
49:32.490 --> 49:34.300
You don’t need to forgive me.

543
49:37.600 --> 49:38.380
But…

544
49:42.110 --> 49:44.170
will you accept my apology?

545
49:57.680 --> 49:58.870
I forgive you.

546
50:15.350 --> 50:16.300
So…

547
50:20.120 --> 50:24.900
you and I,

548
50:26.440 --> 50:28.200
can we still be friends?

549
50:30.390 --> 50:31.400
Sure.

550
50:34.410 --> 50:36.030
But it will take some time.

551
50:39.580 --> 50:40.600
I get it.

552
50:49.880 --> 50:51.570
I have nothing more to say to you.

553
50:53.820 --> 50:54.800
I’m leaving.

554
51:00.580 --> 51:01.300
Bye.

555
51:03.460 --> 51:04.400
Bye.

556
51:47.240 --> 51:50.970
6 MONTHS LATER

557
52:07.830 --> 52:09.300
Whose bride is this?

558
52:09.900 --> 52:11.050
You look beautiful.

559
52:13.170 --> 52:15.400
My bride is also beautiful.

560
52:17.310 --> 52:20.880
Chan, you look so beautiful today that I want to kiss you.

561
52:21.720 --> 52:24.800
You also said that at our wedding last month.

562
52:26.500 --> 52:29.600
You always look beautiful in a wedding dress.

563
52:30.390 --> 52:32.130
I want to kiss you every time you wear a wedding dress.

564
52:33.570 --> 52:34.700
Then kiss me.

565
52:53.150 --> 52:53.920
Ahem.

566
52:55.700 --> 52:57.300
Did I interrupt you?

567
52:58.520 --> 52:59.350
No.

568
53:01.240 --> 53:02.300
Sorry.

569
53:02.930 --> 53:04.760
But I have something to tell you.

570
53:06.730 --> 53:08.530
I’ll go wait outside.

571
53:08.980 --> 53:11.300
It’s okay. You can stay.

572
53:18.700 --> 53:20.700
I want to thank you two very much

573
53:21.540 --> 53:23.100
for holding a wedding again.

574
53:23.700 --> 53:27.050
So I can attend it and congratulate you and Key.

575
53:29.650 --> 53:33.300
This wedding is only for friends and close acquaintances.

576
53:38.190 --> 53:41.750
I’m really happy to see you two getting married.

577
53:44.420 --> 53:45.900
I wish you all the happiness.

578
53:48.150 --> 53:49.230
Thank you.

579
53:50.120 --> 53:51.400
I won’t bother you anymore.

580
53:52.510 --> 53:53.640
See you inside.

581
54:03.210 --> 54:05.100
You are very generous.

582
54:05.950 --> 54:07.180
Don’t you feel jealous?

583
54:09.110 --> 54:10.330
Why would I feel jealous?

584
54:12.460 --> 54:13.830
You are mine now.

585
54:17.850 --> 54:18.800
Yes.

586
54:33.970 --> 54:35.490
Come on. Let’s go inside.

587
54:36.140 --> 54:37.000
Sure.

588
54:45.400 --> 54:49.900
I want to thank you for attending our small wedding today.

589
54:51.010 --> 54:55.600
I’m so happy that everyone is here to share this moment with us.

590
54:58.570 --> 55:01.400
Don’t get drunk yet.

591
55:01.890 --> 55:03.240
I hope you will enjoy the wedding.

592
55:03.680 --> 55:05.560
We are going to sing a song for you. Okay?

593
55:06.400 --> 55:07.490
Please sing along with us.

594
55:26.360 --> 55:30.590
♪ There may be nights when there’s no moon in the sky ♪

595
55:30.920 --> 55:36.700
♪ Days when my heart feels far too tired to try ♪

596
55:36.810 --> 55:41.070
♪ But somehow time led you into my life ♪

597
55:41.390 --> 55:47.000
♪ You unlocked the empty space and let me love you right ♪

598
55:48.560 --> 55:53.300
♪ Feels just like a dream that I found you ♪

599
55:53.720 --> 55:58.400
♪ Every second spent with you is so meaningful ♪

600
55:58.920 --> 56:04.530
♪ The night shines bright, no words could ever do ♪

601
56:04.860 --> 56:07.180
♪ I know that it’s you ♪

602
56:07.440 --> 56:12.900
♪ The word “love” I say to you, I say it to you ♪

603
56:12.970 --> 56:17.460
♪ You’re the shining light when no stars are coming through ♪

604
56:17.500 --> 56:25.600
♪ You’re the key that found its way to my heart ♪

605
56:26.060 --> 56:29.630
♪ Let me love you, love you ♪

606
56:38.650 --> 56:40.170
How do you feel when seeing them?

607
56:41.970 --> 56:43.100
Nothing.

608
56:43.830 --> 56:45.300
They look good together.

609
56:46.550 --> 56:48.810
I mean, do you want to get married when seeing them?

610
56:51.280 --> 56:52.150
No.

611
56:52.680 --> 56:53.870
I was married before.

612
56:54.220 --> 56:55.800
Now, I want to live my own life.

613
57:03.520 --> 57:05.500
Do you want to marry me, little princess?

614
57:09.770 --> 57:12.680
Save this pickup line for another girl, Captain.

615
57:20.500 --> 57:25.950
♪ The word “love” I say to you, I say it to you ♪

616
57:26.030 --> 57:30.500
♪ You’re the shining light when no stars are coming through ♪

617
57:30.540 --> 57:38.700
♪ You’re the key that found its way to my heart ♪

618
57:39.080 --> 57:42.900
♪ Let me love you, love you ♪

619
57:48.990 --> 57:49.720
Game.

620
57:51.090 --> 57:51.900
What’s wrong?

621
57:53.350 --> 57:56.610
I’m just getting emotional to see Miss Chan happy.

622
58:02.170 --> 58:07.520
♪ The word “love” I say to you, I say it to you ♪

623
58:07.770 --> 58:12.250
♪ You’re the shining light when no stars are coming through ♪

624
58:12.280 --> 58:20.390
♪ You’re the key that found its way to my heart ♪

625
58:20.810 --> 58:25.000
♪ Let me love you, love you ♪

626
58:29.310 --> 58:30.250
Kiss her.

627
58:30.400 --> 58:33.140
Kiss her, kiss her, kiss her.

628
58:33.180 --> 58:35.920
Kiss her, kiss her, kiss her.

629
58:35.960 --> 58:38.560
Kiss her, kiss her, kiss her.

630
58:38.600 --> 58:41.100
Kiss her, kiss her, kiss her.

631
58:41.140 --> 58:41.980
Kiss her.

632
58:44.480 --> 58:45.900
Shall we kiss or not?

633
58:47.790 --> 58:48.850
Of course, let’s kiss.

634
58:49.250 --> 58:50.480
What are you waiting for?

635
58:55.400 --> 58:57.640
Everyone. Cheers.

636
58:58.040 --> 58:59.530
Cheers.

637
01:01:01.440 --> 01:01:06.200
My tattoo is you.

638
01:01:12.950 --> 01:01:16.470
My tattoo is also you.

639
01:01:28.270 --> 01:01:29.500
I never imagined

640
01:01:30.980 --> 01:01:32.380
that I would have this day.

641
01:01:40.550 --> 01:01:42.200
I thought…

642
01:01:44.820 --> 01:01:46.600
I could only be your shadow.

643
01:01:51.830 --> 01:01:53.200
Who would have thought

644
01:01:53.550 --> 01:01:56.700
that you and I would get married?

645
01:02:04.450 --> 01:02:05.980
Come to think of it.

646
01:02:07.980 --> 01:02:09.150
Being your shadow…

647
01:02:10.990 --> 01:02:12.300
is not that bad.

648
01:02:16.980 --> 01:02:19.180
I will follow you everywhere

649
01:02:20.840 --> 01:02:23.670
like the shadow of the Moon.

650
01:02:32.700 --> 01:02:34.450
I can’t live without you, Key.

651
01:02:40.570 --> 01:02:42.300
Neither can I.

652
01:02:44.680 --> 01:02:46.260
If there were no moon,

653
01:02:48.700 --> 01:02:50.100
there would be no shadow.

654
01:02:52.020 --> 01:02:53.550
But for me,

655
01:02:56.210 --> 01:02:59.850
there wouldn’t be me without you, Key.

656
01:03:04.660 --> 01:03:06.750
Let’s spend the rest of our lives together,

657
01:03:07.670 --> 01:03:08.900
my wife.

658
01:03:15.230 --> 01:03:18.600
I’m still not used to being called your wife.

659
01:03:20.320 --> 01:03:21.900
You’d better get used to it.

660
01:03:22.780 --> 01:03:25.800
From now on, this is your status.

661
01:03:29.060 --> 01:03:31.300
I got a big promotion.

662
01:03:32.480 --> 01:03:36.900
From being your sugar baby to being your wife.

663
01:03:39.910 --> 01:03:44.130
What should I call you?

664
01:03:51.450 --> 01:03:52.700
You can call me honey.

665
01:03:54.660 --> 01:03:55.750
Can you call me honey?

666
01:03:58.060 --> 01:03:58.900
Yes.

667
01:03:59.630 --> 01:04:00.500
Honey.

668
01:04:02.320 --> 01:04:03.350
Say it again.

669
01:04:05.210 --> 01:04:06.600
Honey.

670
01:04:34.110 --> 01:04:35.260
I love you.

671
01:04:40.460 --> 01:04:41.700
I love you too.

672
01:04:43.010 --> 01:04:43.900
Honey.

673
01:04:43.900 --> 01:04:44.900
MkvDrama.net
